A configuration update applies the wrong values and reports the wrong changes.

A deployment preview merges a base configuration with several overrides. Its six helpers must agree about nested objects, replacement lists, explicit nulls, deletion, and the change report.

The goal

Replace the region list, change only service.timeout, and report those exact setting paths. Preserve explicit nulls, honor deletion directives, validate all inputs, and leave the caller’s data unchanged.

Input to merge_config()
{
  "Base configuration": {
    "service": {
      "host": "api",
      "timeout": 30
    },
    "regions": [
      "us"
    ]
  },
  "Override layers": [
    {
      "service": {
        "timeout": 45
      },
      "regions": [
        "eu"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
Starting code · observed output
{
  "config": {
    "service": {
      "host": "api",
      "timeout": 45
    },
    "regions": [
      "us",
      "eu"
    ]
  },
  "changed": [
    "regions",
    "service"
  ]
}
Required output
{
  "config": {
    "service": {
      "host": "api",
      "timeout": 45
    },
    "regions": [
      "eu"
    ]
  },
  "changed": [
    "regions",
    "service.timeout"
  ]
}
Starting code · config_overlay.py

Lines 35–49 of the original file. The full starting snapshot is available below.

 35  def _overlay(base, patch):
 36      result = deepcopy(base)
 37      for key, incoming in patch.items():
 38          if incoming is None or _deletion(incoming):
 39              result.pop(key, None)
 40          elif type(incoming) is dict:
 41              previous = result.get(key)
 42              result[key] = _overlay(previous if type(previous) is dict else {}, incoming)
 43          elif type(incoming) is list:
 44              result[key] = deepcopy(result.get(key, [])) + deepcopy(incoming) if type(result.get(key)) is list else deepcopy(incoming)
 45          else:
 46              result[key] = incoming
 47      return result
 48  
